{
 "comment": "Golden table for the AIRA-323 command key (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-history-charge-design.md section 5.1, rev 3). Each case: the effective argv (the confine signature is these tokens joined by NUL), the repo identity the client sent (exactly 16 lowercase hex digits or \"none\", the wire rule of spec section 5.1.2; --self-test refuses a table whose inputs break it), and the three keys the daemon stores. The Go key function and the replay script's keys() (docs/dev/aira-history-charge-replay.py --self-test) must both reproduce every case byte for byte. \\u001f (unit separator) divides the repo identity from the argv part. A row with no repo identity gets no key (NULL) and is not a case here.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "plain command",
   "argv": [
    "make",
    "test"
   ],
   "repo": "3f1caaaaaaaaaaaa",
   "want": {
    "key_masked": "3f1caaaaaaaaaaaa\u001fmake|test",
    "key_first4": "3f1caaaaaaaaaaaa\u001fmake|test",
    "key_cmd": "3f1caaaaaaaaaaaa\u001fmake|test"
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "RANT-133: same script, repo A",
   "argv": [
    "./runall.sh"
   ],
   "repo": "3f1caaaaaaaaaaaa",
   "want": {
    "key_masked": "3f1caaaaaaaaaaaa\u001frunall.sh|",
    "key_first4": "3f1caaaaaaaaaaaa\u001frunall.sh|",
    "key_cmd": "3f1caaaaaaaaaaaa\u001frunall.sh|"
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "RANT-133: same script, repo B splits",
   "argv": [
    "./runall.sh"
   ],
   "repo": "9e07bbbbbbbbbbbb",
   "want": {
    "key_masked": "9e07bbbbbbbbbbbb\u001frunall.sh|",
    "key_first4": "9e07bbbbbbbbbbbb\u001frunall.sh|",
    "key_cmd": "9e07bbbbbbbbbbbb\u001frunall.sh|"
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "outside any git repository",
   "argv": [
    "./runall.sh"
   ],
   "repo": "none",
   "want": {
    "key_masked": "none\u001frunall.sh|",
    "key_first4": "none\u001frunall.sh|",
    "key_cmd": "none\u001frunall.sh|"
   }
  },
  {
